# p_alloc_s5: diagnostic. s5 lever set with the allocator pinned (pair of p_alloc_s4; difference =
# graph_clear_values_cpu only).
#
# question   s5_graph_clear_values predicted -17% to -30% from s4's owner census (five largest groups 70%
#            of the peak, weights held several times):
#              534.5 MB  n=3   torch.int64 (28996, 768)     the embedding matrix, THREE times
#              453.0 MB  n=24  torch.int64 (2359296,)       768 x 3072, the FFN weight shape
#              178.2 MB  n=1   torch.int64 (22268928,)      a FOURTH embedding copy, flat
#            duplicates = Graph.forward's values dict (local of forward); the lever drops each value
#            after its last consumer.
# measured   at the line's operating point:
#              s4  leader peaks  2,126,476 / 2,293,620 / 2,340,856   spread 9.35%
#              s5  leader peaks  2,079,588 / 2,321,548 / 2,080,024   spread 11.63%
#            both straddle the allocator modes; leader measure -9.3%, max-over-parties +1.2%: not measured.
# scope      pinned allocator = different operating point (not publishable); decides whether the memory
#            is real.
SHAFT_LEVERS=plaintext_free_cpu,triple_share_free_cpu,trace_nograd_cpu,onnx_single_file_export_cpu,encrypt_spill_cpu,graph_clear_values_cpu
SHAFT_INNER_ENV="MALLOC_ARENA_MAX=1 MALLOC_TRIM_THRESHOLD_=0 MALLOC_MMAP_THRESHOLD_=131072"
